<section id="services">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">What we do</div>
      <h2>Four disciplines, one approval file.</h2>
      <p>Compliance, simulation, and control aren't separate workstreams for a renewable plant — they're read together by the same SLDC reviewer. We run them together too.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="services-grid">
      <div class="service-card reveal">
        <span class="service-num">01</span>
        <h3>CEA &amp; SLDC Approvals</h3>
        <p>Interconnection studies, technical feasibility reports, and approval documentation prepared to the standard your regional SLDC actually expects — not a generic template.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card reveal">
        <span class="service-num">02</span>
        <h3>PSS®E Simulation</h3>
        <p>Load flow, short circuit, and dynamic stability studies for grid-connected solar, wind, and hybrid plants, validated against utility planning models.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card reveal">
        <span class="service-num">03</span>
        <h3>PSCAD Studies</h3>
        <p>Electromagnetic transient modelling for inverter-dominated systems, fault ride-through verification, and protection coordination under IEGC requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card reveal">
        <span class="service-num">04</span>
        <h3>Real-Time Control Integration</h3>
        <p>SCADA, AGC, and AVR set-point design and commissioning support for renewables paired with battery energy storage — built for actual dispatch behaviour, not just the steady-state case.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card reveal">
        <span class="service-num">05</span>
        <h3>Storage-Backed Hybrid Design</h3>
        <p>Sizing, dispatch logic, and grid-code-compliant ramp control for solar/wind plants paired with BESS, modelled end-to-end before a single asset is procured.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card reveal">
        <span class="service-num">06</span>
        <h3>Protection Coordination</h3>
        <p>Relay coordination studies that hold up under fault conditions specific to inverter-based resources — not adapted from synchronous-generator assumptions.</p>
